  "body": "Bugzilla: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=40545\r\nCodepen: https://codepen.io/SaschaNaz/pen/JywOmd\r\nSpec: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-option-element\r\n\r\nIt seems Firefox hasn't support `<select><option label=\"Hey, I'm the label :D\"></option></select>`. The bug in Bugzilla is now at least 18 years old so Mozilla seems to have no intent to implement it. So what's the status of this attribute? Should the behavior be deprecated?\r\n\r\n(Currently even [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en/docs/Web/HTML/Element/option) does not warn or discourage the use of it.)",
